{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/956117-alternative-beast-settings","id":956117,"title":"Alternative Beast Settings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T20:39:05-07:00","id":956117,"title":"Alternative Beast Settings","content":"First of all, this isn't here to reopen old discusion's about the merits/lack there of, of Beast the Primordial.<br /> <br /> The point of this topic is to discuss ways to alter the beast setting, as I was thinking about running a beast game but want a setting that interest me more.<br /> <br /> IDEAS:<br /> <br /> Beast are anti-social. Broods are the exception, not the norm. One of the reasons Beast don't often associate with other Beast is a thing i'm thinking of calling Nightmare Ripples. Basically if more than one Beast is in a neighborhood, city-block, etc, the more likely Nightmare Ripples occur in the Primordial Dream. Nightmare ripples are a phenomenon that causes humans to become resistant to nightmares, and harder to gain Satiety from. They also make Hero's less likely to appear, but cause a sort of emotional deadness in the populace, which occasionally erupts into sporadic fear and paranoia.<br /> <br /> Most Beast are unable to feel strong emotions. Instead of rage they feel indignation, instead of love fondness, greif becomes disappointment, guilt becomes an nagging sense that they have a false understanding of what life is about. The only feeling Beast feel with intensity are Hunger, Fear, and a desire for power. These Beast make up 90% of the Beast population, and experienced the devouring very young, slowly coming into their powers, and never developing strong human attachments. Such Beast tend to have a dry sense of humor, and a philosophical bent. They feed and teach lessons in such a way that reinforces the way they think the world should be, some of them are highly honorable and fair, others are callous, depending on their understanding of the value of ethics, and sense of justice. These are called the Begotten. The other sort of Beast are Devoured later, often in their teens. They maintain more intense human emotions, and rarely develop them beyond the point where they were devoured. These Beast can become monstrous and selfish, or almost fanatically idealistic. Don't have an name for these yet.<br /> <br /> Beast are primarily opposed by Hunters, but Heroes do occasionally arise, often after being driven mad by a dramatic failure on a feeding. The major hunter groups that target Beast are Network Zero (who try to gather information) and Cherion Group (who study captured Beast. Most Atavisms are visible to onlookers when in use. For this reason Beast tend to wear masks when they go out to feed. Most of the time people don't share their experience when they are taught a lesson, or fed on. But the general populance thinks of masked monsters and a popular urban legend.<br /> <br /> That's all I have for now, I might have more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-23-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T21:07:19-07:00","id":956136,"title":"","content":"How about an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956089-perchance-to-dream-the-astral-chronicle-collaborative\">Astral-only</a> Beast story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T21:13:14-07:00","id":956138,"title":"","content":"A setting where the Begotten are the leaders of some sort of strange &quot;Shadow Parliament&quot; might be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T21:13:39-07:00","id":956140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/956117-alternative-beast-settings?p=956136#post956136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about an <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956089-perchance-to-dream-the-astral-chronicle-collaborative&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Astral-only</a> Beast story?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure I understand what such a game would be about, but I do like the idea of people that are physically human that enter dreams to steal people's evil intentions, or plant new ideas in dreamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:33:55-07:00","id":956379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/956117-alternative-beast-settings?p=956140#post956140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely sure I understand what such a game would be about, but I do like the idea of people that are physically human that enter dreams to steal people's evil intentions, or plant new ideas in dreamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a more psycho-nautical exploration of the collective thought-sphere of humanity? The Primordial Dream is just deep-seated fears - what else is out there? <hr /><br /> I had an idea for one that was basically like Ravenloft with the serial numbers filed off, and Dark Lords replaced with Beasts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Remembered another where there are multiple parallel worlds that all &quot;meet up&quot; through the Primordial Dream (and that general region of the Astral). Extra-dimensional psycho-naughts occasionally pass through Chambers... some of which are occupied/incorporated by Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-23-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:14:58-07:00","id":956512,"title":"","content":"Beast dungeon Keeper/evil genius style, the Begotten can create and train minions in their lair send out into the world and advance their goals. The strongest heroes are backed by powerful factions and can only be killed using ways that tie into their backstory and personality (like the super agents in Evil Genius. Keeping their minions happy is required to be a successful beast, kin are the equivalent of the Henchmen units in Evil Genius","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-23-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}